-- §6.3 quiescence drain, INFERRED-scheme half of the `DrainDiags` population
-- (`compiler/types/typecheck.mdk`, #2705 / SA-10a item 17).
--
-- `top`'s scheme is INFERRED, and it quantifies the receiver `Sh a` carries.  At
-- graph quiescence the drain replays that goal with `a` still an unbound `TVar`,
-- and `routeUndeterminedTop`'s `_ => reportAmbiguousImpl` arm reports
-- `T-AMBIGUOUS-INSTANCE` on it because it never asks whether some scheme
-- QUANTIFIES the variable — the `deferrableVarIds`/`goalsClosed` test the sibling
-- T4-warning arm already applies.  That is #3031.
--
-- SPEC ANSWER, hand-derived before running anything: `main` calls `top` at
-- `Bool`, `h` forwards to `needsSh`, `impl Sh Bool` is the unique match, so the
-- program prints 22 on every engine and `check` accepts.  There is no numeric
-- literal anywhere in this file, so nothing here is the undefaulted-`Num` class
-- #2646 owes — the ambiguity the drain sees is manufactured by the drain.
--
-- WHAT THIS ROW PINS: `check` must NOT report `T-AMBIGUOUS-INSTANCE`.  Today it
-- does not, because `DrainRollback` discards the drain's diagnostics on every
-- check driver.  The day the drain residual reaches a shipped verb — the T4
-- census ruling #2665 asks for — this row goes RED, which is the signal that
-- `DrainDiags`'s deletion condition has moved.
interface Sh a where
  shv : a -> Int

impl Sh Int where
  shv _ = 11

impl Sh Bool where
  shv _ = 22

needsSh : Sh a => a -> Int
needsSh x = shv x

top a = h a
  where
    h x = needsSh x

main = println (top True)
